Field Note 0004
Classification

I originally organized these notes by subject.

Environment.

History.

Witness testimony.

Scientific literature.

Personal observations.

It seemed sensible.

It also failed.

The most interesting relationships consistently ignored those boundaries.

Documents concerning environmental degradation frequently intersected with discussions of technological development.

Witness testimony often raised questions better addressed by cognitive science than by folklore.

Historical material repeatedly refused to remain confined to history.

Eventually I stopped asking:

"What is this document about?"

Instead I began asking:

"What role does this document play?"

That small change reorganized everything.

The structure became less intuitive.

It also became considerably more useful.

I still do not know why.